“With the support of the United Kingdom’s government, donors, national governments and global citizens such as you, we can put the social iniquity of malnutrition into historical archives,” Tracey Ullman, Ambassador of the Power of the Ealm.
The group also stated that, after carrying out more than q. q. , the United Kingdom called for an improvement in maternal and child's diet, the government has said it would co-finance the Power of Nutrition project, which will reach 5 million women and children through dietary measures.
Responding to one of the FAQs on the website, “Why do you think we can end extreme poverty?’
the Global Citizen movement said: “It will be a long and hard road – sometimes we’re going to fail.
